{uses:3_0-preface.lbl}
' Image BBS 128: i/su.config, the new-system setup: its menu.
' im loads it at line 4000 and calls it (3240-3242), with lm = the option
' picked: 1 configure, 2 convert from 1.2, 3 convert from 2.0.
'
' 11/05/2026: a menu of parts instead of one fixed run of questions (the
' setup redesign: ImageBBS3 TODO.md; Image-128 issue #1). Each part is a
' sub.* module, modules/sub.su.*.lbl, which im loads at 60000 (gosub 74)
' while this stays in memory at 4000: so the parts can gosub the shared
' lines at 4900 on (modules/su_helpers.lbl numbers them for the parts).
' Only this module loads sub.* modules: a part that needs sub.info or
' sub.clocks leaves a request (su%(9)) and this calls them after it returns
' (a sub.* loading another hits the 128's nested-reload bug, TODO).
' im's program area is 32K: im is 15K, sub.clocks 9K, so this stays small.
'
' Setup's own variables (DIMmed in init, after im 3200's &,27,1, so im
' 3087's &,28,1 drops the arrays when setup is over):
'   su%(1-4)   1 when part 1-4 is done; su%(9) clock follow-ups wanted
'   su%(31-36), (37-38), (43-47), (49-53): 1 when that item of part 1-4
'              (drives, clock, sysop, BBS) has been asked; ib = the part's
'              base (24+6*part), nx/nx$ its first item not asked yet
'   su%(10)    the boot device; su%(11-16), su%(21-26) the chosen device and
'              drive of drives 1-6 (dv%() and dr%() stay the boot drive
'              until sub.su.write, so modules load from the boot disk)
'   su$(1-5)   sysop: handle, password, first and last name, e-mail
'   su$(6-10)  BBS: name, main prompt, chat entry, chat exit, new user credits
'   su$(11-13) clock: method (ck$), time zone (tz$), the method's name
' Built with C64List 4.04 (BASIC 2 tokens, which BASIC 7 runs; 4.06 won't
' take the numeric {assign}s).
{alpha:alt}
{include:quoters.lbl}
{include:"asm\equates.asm"}
{assign:3084	=3084	} ' im: reopen the command channel, read bd.data (c64 3.0: 3080)
{assign:3200	=3200	} ' im: insert-disks menu
{assign:3300	=3300	} ' im: start the daily log
{assign:3404	=3404	} ' im: boot frame: show z3$
{assign:3414	=3414	} ' im: boot frame: clear the lines under it
{step:2}

{number:4000}
	rem "i/su.config" {usedef:__BuildDate} {usedef:__BuildTime}
' 11/05/2026: the window's top at row 6 for all of setup, so nothing printed
' under im's boot frame (rows 2-5) can scroll it away: Image's console scrolls
' from sctop, and im 3404 redraws only the frame's two lines, not its border
' 11/06/2026: dv% (the current device: the last gosub 2's) set back to the
' boot device (su%(10)): im 3084 opens bd.data on dv%, and setup's last
' steps (the daily log, drive 3) left it at a CMD HD's 9: no bd.data
' there, so im showed the start-up menu again
	poke {sym:sctop},6:on lm gosub {:new},{:conv12},{:conv20}:poke {sym:sctop},.:poke {sym:timeset},su%(7):dv%=su%(10):return

{nice:100}
' 1: a new system
{:new}
	gosub {:init}
' the menu: the parts, each with a checkmark in front of its number once done; Return takes the
' first not done, then the review (tools/setup_test.py presses Return at
' every prompt)
{:menu}
	gosub 3414:z3$="Image BBS 128 Setup":gosub 3404:&"{f6}{white}"
	n=.:restore {:names}:for i=1 to np:read a$:a%=i:b$=mid$(" {$ba}",su%(i)+1,1)+" "
	if n=. and su%(i)=. then n=i
	&"{white}{pound}$b{yellow}{pound}%a{lt. blue}) {pound}$a{f6}":next
	&"{yellow}  R{lt. blue}) Review{comma} then write system files{f6:2}":a$="Review"
	if n then restore {:names}:for i=1 to n:read a$:next
' 11/06/2026: {pound}i1's length is 53252's: set here, not left from the last input
	poke 53252,1:&"{lt. green}Return{colon} {pound}$a{f6}{yellow}Your choice{colon} {white}{pound}i1{f6}"
	a=val(an$):if an$=r$ or an$="" then a=n:if n=. then an$="R"
	if an$="R" or an$="r" then gosub {:review}:on a goto {:menu}:return
	if a<1 or a>np then {:menu}
	on a gosub {:drives},{:clock},{:sysop},{:bbs}:goto {:menu}
' the parts, in the menu's order; "" ends them, and init counts them (np),
' so a new part is a name here and its label in the two "on a gosub" lists
' (the menu's and the review's). Room: su%(part) is its done flag (su%(7)
' on are taken: parts 1-6), su%(24+6*part)+ its items' checks (su%() is
' DIMmed 60: a sixth part needs more). 11/07/2026
{:names}
	data "Devices and Drives","Clock and Time Zone","Sysop Information","BBS Information",""

{nice:100}
' the parts: each a sub.su.* module (goto 74: its return is this gosub's)
' the bus scan first (sub.sysdos im=2: each device's model in tt$(8-30)),
' which the Drives part lists and checks the picks against
{:drives}
	im=2:a$="sysdos":gosub 74:im=1:a$="su.drives":goto 74
{:sysop}
	im=1:a$="su.sysop":goto 74
{:bbs}
	im=1:a$="su.bbs":goto 74
' the clock's method, then, if it asks (su%(9)), the system time zone (sub.info
' im=8: into tz$, e.data record 45) and the alarms that make the idle screen
' check daylight saving time when its rule changes the clock (sub.clocks
' im=15: none if the zone has no DST)
' the zone list (37 zones, more than the 18 rows under the frame) scrolls
' under it only (sctop, 4000), and sub.info pauses it every 14 lines (the
' More prompt is off on the console: moreprmt returns when local)
{:clock}
	su%(9)=.:im=1:a$="su.clock":gosub 74:if su%(9)=. then return
	y%=val(su$(11)):gosub 3414:im=8:gosub 447:su$(12)=tz$
' 11/06/2026: then back to the Clock part's menu (it returns when done);
' the zone is asked only once one was chosen (Return at Which One? leaves it)
	im=15:a$="clocks":gosub 74:su%(37)=1:su%(38)=-(su$(12)<>""):goto {:clock}

{nice:100}
' R: a part not done yet is done first (a = 1: back to the menu); then
' the answers, to change or continue, and the files written (sub.su.write;
' a = 0: setup is over)
{:review}
	if n then a=n:on a gosub {:drives},{:clock},{:sysop},{:bbs}:a=1:return
' 11/05/2026: the drives as the Drives part's table (sub.su.drives im=2:
' labels, devices, models, disk names), after a scan (the zone list's tt$()
' wrote over the last one's).
' 11/06/2026: numbered as the menu's parts: a number runs that part and
' comes back here; C (or Return) writes the files. 18 rows in 40 columns:
' the table's 13 (its heading "1) Drive"), the Clock's 2 (the method, then
' the zone: one line in 80 columns), Sysop, BBS, the question
{:review1}
	gosub 3414:z3$="Review":gosub 3404
	im=2:a$="sysdos":gosub 74:im=2:a$="su.drives":gosub 74
	b$="(none chosen)":if su$(12)<>"" then gosub {:su.zone}
	a$="{f6}   ":if sw>79 then a$="{comma} "
	&"{yellow}2{lt. blue}) Clock{colon} {white}"+su$(13)+a$+b$+"{f6}"
	&"{yellow}3{lt. blue}) Sysop{colon} {white}"+su$(1)+"{f6}{yellow}4{lt. blue}) BBS{colon} {white}"+su$(6)+"{f6}"
	poke 53252,1:&"{yellow}Number to change{comma} or [C]ontinue{colon} {white}{pound}i1{f6}":a=val(an$)
	if a>. and a<=np then on a gosub {:drives},{:clock},{:sysop},{:bbs}:goto {:review1}
	if an$<>"C" and an$<>"c" and an$<>"" then {:review1}
	im=1:a$="su.write":gosub 74
	gosub 3414:gosub {:su.copr}:lp=1:&"{f6:2}Be sure to enter {quotation}IM{quotation} once online to complete the configuration of "
	lp=1:&"your BBS. Message bases{comma} U/D and U/X libraries can be configured by using "
	lp=1:&"the {quotation}Base Editors{quotation} option.{f6:2}"+c$+"{f6:2}"
' esc-p: clear to start of line
' (then the lines under the frame cleared: if im shows its start-up menu
' again, the closing screen isn't left under it)
	lp=1:&"Hit any key to continue{colon} {pound}g1"+es$+"p":gosub 3414:a=.:return

{nice:100}
' 2, 3: convert an Image BBS 64 system (sub.su.convert). Its d.data not
' found, the sysop can set up a new system instead (a = 1)
{:conv12}
	gosub {:init}:im=1:a$="su.convert":gosub 74:if a then {:menu}
	gosub {:clock}:im=2:a$="su.convert":goto 74
{:conv20}
	gosub {:init}:im=3:a$="su.convert":gosub 74:if a then {:menu}
	return

{nice:100}
' setup's variables, and every drive the boot drive for now (on a new system
' dv%(1-6) are 0: im 3087 found no bd.data); drive 0 (d1%, d2%) is the boot
' drive throughout (im line 2). The boot device is dv%, which im 3242 has
' just loaded this from: bootdev ($1800) is 0 by now (a ?load error,
' 11/05/2026)
{:init}
' define esc for screen editor tricks:
' esc-@: clear from cursor position to bottom of screen
' esc-p: clear from cursor position to beginning of line
' esc-q: clear from cursor position to end of line
	es$=chr$(27)
	dim su%(60),su$(20):bv=dv%:if bv<8 then bv=8
' stop the status line flashing "set time" during setup (timeset: 0 flashes,
' irqhn.asm irq1); its old value kept in su%(7) (after the dim) and put back at 4000's exit,
' as i/lo.idle reads it as "the clock is set" (AutoMaint, 4210-4211)
	su%(7)=peek({sym:timeset}):poke {sym:timeset},1
	su%(10)=bv:d1%=bv:d2%=.
	for i=1 to 6:dv%(i)=bv:dr%(i)=.:su%(10+i)=bv:su%(20+i)=.:next
' 11/07/2026: the number of parts (np), from the names, not written in
	np=.:restore {:names}
{:count}
	read a$:if a$<>"" then np=np+1:goto {:count}
	d1$="12011111201":return

' shared lines for the parts (modules/su_helpers.lbl numbers them for them)
' su.ask: ask p$, w$ the default (Return takes it), ln long, pl the case.
' &,1,32 (edit mode): the default shown after the prompt, then the prompt
' again on the next line, for the answer: typing replaces the default.
' (11/06/2026: &,1,16, the default in the input itself, was tried: typing
' added to it, "8" then 9 gave "89")
{number:4900}
{:su.ask}
	poke 53252,ln:b$=w$:&,1,32:if an$="" then an$=b$
	return
' su.item: a part's menu line: a% its number, a$ its label, b$ its value;
' a check if asked (su%(ib+a%)); the first not asked is nx, nx$ its label
' (set nx=. first)
{number:4910}
{:su.item}
	ic=su%(ib+a%):if ic=. and nx=. then nx=a%:nx$=a$
	&"{white}"+mid$(" {$ba}",ic+1,1)+" {yellow}{pound}%a{lt. blue}) "+left$(a$+"..................",18)+"{colon} {white}{pound}$b{f6}":return
' su.pick: a = the item to ask: the number typed (1-h), or Return's: the
' first not asked (nx); 0 = done (D, or Return when all were asked: the
' rest keep their defaults). 11/06/2026: Return walks the items in order
{number:4920}
{:su.pick}
	poke 53252,1:a$="Done":if nx then a$=nx$
	&"{f6}{yellow}1-{pound}!h{comma} D(one){comma} Return{equal}{lt. green}{pound}$a{yellow}{colon} {white}{pound}i1{f6}":a=val(an$)
	if an$="" then a=nx:return
	if an$="D" or an$="d" then a=.:return
	on -(a<1 or a>h) goto {:su.pick}:return
' su.create, su.done: 'Creating "f$"...', then "Done!"
{number:4930}
{:su.create}
	&"{lt. blue}Creating {quotation}{cyan}{pound}$f{lt. blue}{quotation}...":return
{number:4932}
{:su.done}
	&"{white}Done!{f6}":return
' su.copr: the copyright line, in one place (bd.data, the closing screen)
{number:4940}
{:su.copr}
	c$="Image 128 Copyright 2026 New Image Software":return
' su.zone: b$ = the time zone (su$(12)) readably: "MST -7:00/MDT", its UTC
' offset and daylight name, not its code (s.timezones: name, hhmm from
' UTC-12, DST rule letter, DST name): 13 characters, for a 40-column line.
' 11/06/2026 (from sub.su.clock, for the review too)
{number:4950}
{:su.zone}
	z$=su$(12):b=val(mid$(z$,4,2))*60+val(mid$(z$,6,2))-720:b$=mid$("-+",-(b>=.)+1,1):b=abs(b)
	b$=left$(z$,3)+" "+b$+mid$(str$(int(b/60)),2)+":"+right$("0"+mid$(str$(b-int(b/60)*60),2),2)
	if mid$(z$,8,1)<>"-" then b$=b$+"/"+mid$(z$,9,3)
	return

	rem copr. 1996 new image 5/5/96-rwp
	rem "i/su.config (c)nissa 2020-06-14 lh+ad. 2022-10-11, 2026-11-05 rs"
